#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.12"
# dependencies = ["playwright==1.63.0", "platformdirs==4.12.2", "cmake==4.4.3", "ninja==1.13.2", "libclang==18.1.1", "psutil==7.2.2", "numpy==2.3.5", "matplotlib==3.10.8", "pillow==12.3.0", "onnx==1.19.1", "protobuf==6.32.1", "ml-dtypes==0.5.1"]
# ///
"""Complete standalone strict-FP32 browser ConvTranspose spatial-MR milestone.

Run: uv run --script voicevox_core_benchmark.py --output ct-report
Embedded offline tests (after dependencies are installed): add --self-test
Source preparation only: add --prepare-only (downloads/builds, no inference).
Plan only: add --dry-run (no downloads, compilation, browser or inference).

All source helpers, patches, provenance pins, tests, browser workers and reporting
code are embedded and hash-verified. No adjacent source files are required.
This milestone is Linux x86-64 only and requires a C/C++ compiler and Chromium system
libraries. It installs pinned Rust 1.96.0 / Emscripten 4.0.8 under its private cache.
First execution may use several GB and take two hours. Chromium is installed via
Playwright 1.63.0; its engine major version must be 153. The script never installs
system packages; on Linux prepare those separately with Playwright install-deps.

Conditions: common forced strict loadsplat and exact-inplace LeakyRelu fix,
original CT / unmodified rebuilt CT / narrow CT spatial-MR candidate. Normal-tier
revectorization OFF, strict FP32, fixed fixture962, XNN2 / ORT1, seed1729.
Only actual measured browser calls may populate the 45-call result. No simulated
measurements or CPU time-series claims. Untimed correctness, provider assignment,
and separate instrumented CT callback diagnostics precede primary measurement.

Public output is summary.json plus standalone report.html only. Raw audio, raw
FP32 buffers, tensors, model files, arbitrary exception messages and logs are
never public outputs. Downloads/build logs and models stay in a private cache;
no network uploads, GitHub writes, code signing or precision changes occur.
"""
